WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.329
DEXPit is a card battler from Engines of Creation.

00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:08.508
With Founding Packs, its HexPit prototype turns one familiar action into a market launch.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.727
The first player opens a pack.

00:00:10.727 --> 00:00:15.536
By the twelfth pack, the game has a stablecoin trading pool on Flap.

00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:19.043
Open the public replay and select pack one.

00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:22.129
Five test dollars bought these five collectible cards.

00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:25.600
The same receipt assigned just over seventy-six thousand GAME.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.528
Pack order sets that amount.

00:00:27.528 --> 00:00:31.000
The card draw determines which cards the player owns.

00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:33.274
Now select the final mint.

00:00:33.274 --> 00:00:35.453
Twelve packs raised sixty test dollars.

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:41.991
In one transaction, the Flap Portal created GAME and paired the entire raise with five hundred thousand GAME.

00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:45.624
The other half of the supply went to pack buyers.

00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:49.619
If a round expires below target, buyers can request a refund.

00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:53.364
The launch and claim are public on BNB Smart Chain testnet.

00:00:53.364 --> 00:01:00.011
Open the final mint receipt to inspect the pool, then the claim receipt to see the test buyer collect the player reserve.

00:01:00.011 --> 00:01:03.938
Our second launcher gives reviewers a separate round to try with a wallet.

00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:07.937
For Flap, the opportunity extends beyond one card game.

00:01:07.937 --> 00:01:11.896
Our next studio title could sell a starter kit instead.

00:01:11.896 --> 00:01:15.459
Its designers would change the items and sale rules.

00:01:15.459 --> 00:01:21.001
The engineers could reuse the factory pattern, stablecoin collection, pool settlement, and transaction history.

00:01:21.001 --> 00:01:24.960
The shipped prototype demonstrates that path with DEX Pit cards.

00:01:25.416 --> 00:01:31.118
Explore the twelve receipts without signing in, or connect a testnet wallet to the second round.

00:01:31.118 --> 00:01:34.682
The playable demo, launcher source, and transaction proofs are public.

00:01:34.682 --> 00:01:38.958
This is Engines of Creation's proposal for bringing more games to Flap.
